-- =============================================================================
-- Pattern Matching: wide multi-column decision table (regression test)
--
-- Regression guard for the fall-through desugaring. Each non-final clause here
-- has several distinguishable (literal) columns. The original desugaring inlined
-- the desugaring of the ENTIRE remaining clause tail into every WHEN/OTHERWISE,
-- so the generated CONSIDER tree grew multiplicatively and `l4 check` on a table
-- this size took well over a minute. The linear desugaring binds each
-- fall-through once (via a nullary LET ... IN), so this now checks in well under
-- a second. Keep this table modest so CI stays quick.
-- =============================================================================

IMPORT prelude

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
      e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE tariff 0 1 2 3 4 IS 10
DECIDE tariff 1 2 3 4 5 IS 20
DECIDE tariff 2 3 4 5 6 IS 30
DECIDE tariff 3 4 5 6 7 IS 40
DECIDE tariff 4 5 6 7 8 IS 50
DECIDE tariff 5 6 7 8 9 IS 60
DECIDE tariff 0 1 2 3 4 IS 999   -- shadowed by the first clause (first match wins)
DECIDE tariff a b c d e IS 0     -- catch-all

#EVAL tariff 0 1 2 3 4   -- 10 (first match wins, not 999)
#EVAL tariff 3 4 5 6 7   -- 40
#EVAL tariff 5 6 7 8 9   -- 60
#EVAL tariff 9 9 9 9 9   -- 0 (catch-all)
